    "6753973e-c4ef-4c30-8d92-0cc58d4e7063": {
      "type": "founder-text-section",
      "settings": {
        "background": "#ffffff",
        "subtitle": "ABOUT THE FOUNDER",
        "title": "In 2005, Anna-Mieke had the vision to create a conflict-free diamond and has led the evolution of the lab-grown diamond industry ever since.",
        "text": "<p><b>Anna-Mieke Anderson (pronounced Anna-Meeka)</b> is the Founder and CEO of MiaDonna & Company, an award-winning, eco-friendly fine jewelry brand based in Portland, Oregon. Named after her daughter Mia and mother Donna, MiaDonna was founded in 2005 with a bold mission: to modernize a male-dominated, ethically troubled industry by creating a conflict-free, sustainable alternative to mined diamonds.</p>\n\n<p>After learning the origin of her own earth-mined diamond, Anna-Mieke became driven to find a truly ethical solution—and discovered the answer wasn’t in the ground, but in the lab. She became one of the earliest visionaries behind lab-grown diamonds, developing stones that are not only free from conflict but superior in quality and sustainability.</p>\n\n<p>Anna-Mieke is now internationally recognized as a pioneering force in the lab-grown diamond industry, and a passionate environmental and humanitarian activist. Her work has earned widespread acclaim for challenging outdated norms and advocating for a more responsible jewelry standard.</p>\n\n<p>She also founded The Greener Diamond Foundation, which funds education, mentorship, and agriculture programs in diamond mining communities—empowering people who have long suffered the consequences of conflict diamonds. Anna-Mieke personally leads missions to these regions, ensuring lasting impact and sustainable change.</p>\n\n<p>Originally from New Zealand and raised in Australia, Anna-Mieke moved to the U.S. at 19 and now lives in Portland, Oregon. She continues her work as a devoted mother, entrepreneur, and changemaker committed to a better future for people and the planet.</p>\n\n<p>In 2025, after two decades of building MiaDonna—disrupting an industry, challenging the status quo, and proving that luxury and ethics can not only coexist, but thrive—Anna-Mieke decided to step away from MiaDonna to set her sights on a new mission: empowering women into leadership to create lasting global, social, and environmental impact.</p>"
      }
    },
